2026-11-06T02:59:24.6878067Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6886122Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6886480Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6886711Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6886825Z 
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6886941Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6887137Z 
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6887300Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6887647Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6887835Z 
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6887934Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6888174Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6888335Z 
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6888488Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:59:24.6888802Z   $ sh ./install-nix
